owing that when A and B are independent eve"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-maths-b-06-s12","code":"6.12","title":"Determination of the probability of two or more independent events The use of tree diagrams will be"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-maths-b-06-s13","code":"6.13","title":"Understand and use the term ‘expected frequency’"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-maths-b-06-s14","code":"6.14","title":"reasonable adjustment for a particular student may be unique to that individual and therefore might"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-maths-b-06-s15","code":"6.15","title":"modular qualification will be divided into a number of units. Each unit will have its own assessment"}]', 6, '2026-11-25T18:00:00.000Z', '2026-11-25T18:00:00.000Z');
