.12","title":"understand how vector quantities differ from scalar quantities"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s13","code":"1.13","title":"understand that force is a vector quantity"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s14","code":"1.14","title":"calculate the resultant force of forces that act along a line"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s15","code":"1.15","title":"know that friction is a force that opposes motion"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s16","code":"1.16","title":"know and use the relationship between unbalanced force, mass and acceleration:"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s17","code":"1.17","title":"know and use the relationship between weight, mass and gravitational field strength:"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s18","code":"1.18","title":"know that the stopping distance of a vehicle is made up of the sum of the thinking"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s19","code":"1.19","title":"describe the factors affecting vehicle stopping distance, including speed, mass, road"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s20","code":"1.20","title":"describe the forces acting on falling objects (and explain why falling objects reach a"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s21","code":"1.21","title":"practical: investigate how extension varies with applied force for helical springs, metal"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s22","code":"1.22","title":"know that the initial linear region of a force-extension graph is associated with"},{"id":"topic-edx-igcse-phys-01-s23","code":"1.23","title":"describe elastic behaviour as the ability of a material to recover its original shape"}]', 1, '2026-11-25T18:00:00.000Z', '2026-11-25T18:00:00.000Z');
